  "change": {
    "scope": "Dependency bool table plus SourceLayerBounds, SourceImageBounds and RequiredSourceBounds metadata scratch; ParameterCaptureBounds forwards the allocation-free contract.",
    "bound": "Ordinary definition admission limits graphs to 256 primitives. The largest bound-table storage is 12 KiB: three tables of 256 rectangles, 16 bytes each. Queries return before recursive pixel capture; no retained cache, owner or field is introduced.",
    "initialization": "Forward region/bounds/storage and dependency slots are assigned before use under earlier-input admission. Backward requests are explicitly cleared before accumulation. The optional stored-input extent table remains conditional.",
    "ownership": "Stack scratch has no managed storage reservation. Actual playback pixel tables, images, surfaces and their refusal/cancellation/retry paths retain their existing ownership.",
    "internalConsumers": "Remove query-only RenderBudget parameters and migrate all internal consumers together, including capture-hint forwarding. Published signatures remain unchanged.",
    "tests": "Nine direct warmed-allocation contracts cover zero, one and256 nodes, including optional stored-input planning. Existing graph borrowing/cancellation/retry is retained; obsolete metadata heap-refusal and disconnected scratch-budget assertions are replaced or removed. All numerical inputs/assertions and actual pixel-storage refusal paths remain."
